{"id":"ks-23","slug":"ks-23","name":"KS-23","aliases":["KS23","Ks-23m","TOZ-123"],"kind":"firearm","category":"shotguns","subcategory":"Soviet pump-action heavy shotgun","description":"The KS-23 is a pump action shotgun manufactured by Russian company Tula Arms Plant. The KS-23 was developed by TsNIITochMash in the Soviet Union for use by the Ministry of Internal Affairs. It is officially designated as a carbine in Russia because it uses a rifled barrel.","history":"The KS-23 was designed in the 1970s by TsNIITochMash, a key weapons developer in the Soviet Union, as a shotgun for the Ministry of Internal Affairs (MVD) with the purpose of suppressing prison riots. The design implemented barrels produced for the Gryazev-Shipunov GSh-23, an autocannon that fires 23×115mm rounds fitted to Soviet military aircraft. These GSh-23 barrels were rejected by quality control due to manufacturing flaws, but were deemed to be acceptable for the lower stress of firing slugs and less-lethal rounds. These barrels were then cut down in length for the KS-23, reducing production costs, and a 23x75mm shell was developed. As a result of reusing GSh-23 barrels, the KS-23 has the unique features of being a shotgun with a rifled barrel.\nThe KS-23 began to see use during the mid-1980s by several MVD forces, including the Militsiya and the Internal Troops. During the 1990s, research was made into improving the original design to make it usable in confined indoor areas. Two prototypes were proposed, the KS-23M and KS-23K, although only the M version saw use.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":"23×75mmR"},{"label":"Action","value":"Pump action, multilugged rotating bolt"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"3+1 shells in underbarrel tube (KS-23)"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"7 shell detachable box magazine (KS-23K)"},{"label":"Sights","value":"Front blade, rear notch."}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Length","value":"1040 mm (KS-23)","numeric":1040,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Length","value":"650-875 mm (KS-23M, without/with stock)"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"510 mm (KS-23)","numeric":510,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"350 mm (KS-23M)","numeric":350,"unit":"mm"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Effective Range","value":"150 m (KS-23, KS-23M)","numeric":150,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Effective Range","value":"100 m (KS-23k)","numeric":100,"unit":"m"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designer","value":"TsNIITochMash"},{"label":"Designed","value":"1971–early 1980s"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Tula Arms Plant"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1985–present"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"Soviet Union"},{"label":"In Service","value":"1985–present"}]}],"specIndex":{"Cartridge":"23×75mmR","Action":"Pump action, multilugged rotating bolt","Feed System":"3+1 shells in underbarrel tube (KS-23)","Sights":"Front blade, rear notch.","Length":"1040 mm (KS-23)","Barrel Length":"510 mm (KS-23)","Effective Range":"150 m (KS-23, KS-23M)","Designer":"TsNIITochMash","Designed":"1971–early 1980s","Manufacturer":"Tula Arms Plant","Produced":"1985–present","Origin":"Soviet Union","In Service":"1985–present"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B1%D0%B8%D0%BD_%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%9A%D0%A1-23%D0%9C_%D0%94%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B4%2C_%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%B4_%D1%81%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B7_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B0_01.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B1%D0%B8%D0%BD_%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%9A%D0%A1-23%D0%9C_%D0%94%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B4,_%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%B4_%D1%81%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%B7_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B0_01.jpg","width":2107,"hei